@startuml 10-ca-rotation
!include theme-oriolrius.puml
title Rotating a CA
hide empty description
[*] --> active
state "active\n(signs new certificates)" as active <<good>>
state "rotating\n(still trusted, signs nothing)" as rotating <<warn>>
state "retired\n(no longer trusted)" as retired <<bad>>
active --> rotating : Rotate\n(a new active CA is created)
rotating --> retired : Retire, after its\ncertificates have expired
retired --> [*]
note right of rotating
  During the overlap the trust files list BOTH keys.
  Deploy the new trust files first: a server without the
  new key rejects certificates from the new CA.
end note
@enduml
